menu "FTM time engine"

config FTM_TIME_ENGINE
    bool "Measure gPTP time over FTM as a Wi-Fi coprocessor station"
    depends on HOSTED_AVB_CLOCK_LINK && HOSTED_AVB_BUILD_COPROCESSOR_HANDLER
    default n
    help
        For a Wi-Fi coprocessor that is a station (an endpoint's standby
        link). While associated, it asks the access point for a PTP
        compatible FTM burst every 125 ms, reads gPTP time from the
        Follow_Up the responder puts in each frame, and sends the host
        gPTP time against the clock link's timer. Needs
        CONFIG_ESP_WIFI_ENABLE_FTM_PTP (Espressif's PTP compatible FTM)
        and a responder that fills the Follow_Up. Enable
        HOSTED_AVB_WIFI_TIME on the host.

endmenu
